extends RefCounted
## The watch-through's scenes, from story/YESTERYEAR_SHORT.md (our own telling - new dialogue throughout).
##
## Each scene: "set" (Sets.gd), optional "title", "cast" {who: [spot, facing_deg]}, "camera" [from, look] for
## the opening shot, and "beats" (see WatchThrough._beat). Spots are names the set defines (Sets.SPOTS) or a
## Vector3 relative to the set's anchor. Change a line here and it changes in the game.
##
## Facing: 0 = towards +Z, 90 = towards +X. Camera looks can be "@who" (follows that person).
## ["shot", who, with, kind] frames a conversation from where people actually stand (WatchThrough._shot):
## "ots" over with's shoulder onto who, "close", "two", "wide".
## A line can carry {to, mood, style, gesture}: who they speak to ("-" = nobody in particular), a face
## (happy, amused, sad, worried, stern, annoyed, surprised, curious, skeptical; "" = neutral), a talking style
## (calm, lively, argue, sad) and a nod / head_shake.

